; unsaturated hydrocarbons: CnH2n. contains at least one C=C double bond.
; the double bond is the reactive site — it is a functional group.
; planar geometry at the double bond (sp2 hybridisation). cannot rotate.
; cis/trans isomers: groups locked on same (cis) or opposite (trans) sides.
; naming: ethene (C2H4, ethylene), propene (C3H6), butene (C4H8).
; addition reactions: Br2, H2, H2O, HCl add across the double bond.
; ethene + H2 → ethane (hydrogenation — catalytic, industrial)
; ethene + H2O → ethanol (hydration — industrial route to ethanol)
; polymerisation: ethylene → polyethylene (PE). propylene → polypropylene (PP).
; ethylene is the most produced organic chemical in industry.
; plant hormone: ethylene triggers fruit ripening.

